Z||000005||rodmcneill||02-21-2001||12:52 AM||||The X-11 was the performance version of the Chevy Citation, the car that gave its front suspension to our Fiero's rear. I had thought about doing the "true roller rocker arm" on my GT, namely the Gold Cranes, this is what I remember from it. First thing I found is that they will not fit! The Fiero valve covers are not tall enough to accept a roller rocker arm. This is why you see alot of guys using the Comp.Cams roller tip rocker arms, they must be close to the original rocker dimensions. Also on the Crane rocker arms the kit also came with new threaded studs for the heads. The old pressed in rocker studs had to be removed, the holes threaded and the new studs installed. There are also higher grade roller rocker arms out there besides the Gold Cranes.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||02-21-2001||01:08 AM||||I was running Fiero valve covers on the X-11 with the Crane Rollers. They fit.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rodmcneill||02-21-2001||01:35 AM||||Sorry about the mis-information of them not fitting under the valve covers..its been a couple of years since I thought about it. I think it was someone at The Fiero Store that told me that they would not fit.||||reg||1
